<title>JAPAN: Japan September pork imports down 39.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan September pork imports down 39.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in September totalled 28,229 tonnes, down 39.1 percent from 46,373 tonnes in September 1995, Finance Ministry data showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   September 96   August 96    September 95</p>
<p> Total	     28,229	 28,449	 46,373</p>
<p> Refrigerated    13,464	 15,835	 15,344</p>
<p> Frozen	    14,765	 12,614	 31,029</p>
<p> Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     7,093	  8,040	  7,250</p>
<p> U.S.		 5,303	  6,733	  7,340</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    September 96  August 96    September 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	     7,397	  4,602	 14,212</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in the first nine months of calendar 1996 totalled 129,979 tonnes, against 123,964 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in the first nine months of calendar 1996 came to 406,251 tonnes, against 288,460 tonnes in the same period of 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
